{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_34","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"export POSE_REVIEW_CLI=/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-ready\ncat <<'POSE_DRAFT_INPUT' | \\\"\"'$POSE_REVIEW_CLI\" review draft-check --draft -\ndecision: changes-requested\n\nN1 is a medium blocker at [accepted_limits.go:28](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-1368568676/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits.go:28). The reason matcher searches for “Accepted because” anywhere in the text, so “Not accepted because this would violate scope” supplies several letter runs after the substring and passes ready-check. That contradicts R1/R4: the declared limit itself says it is not accepted. The focused Go tests passed: go -C pose-mcp test ./internal/pose ./internal/cli -run '\"'AcceptedLimit|WithinASealedLimit|ReadyCheckJudges|Brief|Conclud'. The required validation commands could not compile because the read-only sandbox blocks Go build/cache writes; sealed build and unit evidence is cited below.\n\n| Criterion | Result | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|\n| assumption-integrity | failed (N1) | N1; pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits.go:28 |\n| backend-concurrency | passed | unit:pose-mcp/go/test |\n| backend-contracts | passed | integration:pose-mcp/go/review-brief-conclusion-rules-integration |\n| backend-input-errors | failed (N1) | N1 |\n| backend-integration-impact | passed | integration:pose-mcp/go/review-bundle-convergence |\n| backend-observability | passed | unit:pose-mcp/go/test |\n| compatibility | passed | integration:pose-mcp/go/review-brief-templates-are-immutable-integration |\n| correctness | failed (N1) | N1 |\n| design-causality | passed | structure:design-83948b834dad4e0e |\n| documentation | passed | integration:pose-mcp/go/review-brief-templates-are-immutable-integration |\n| operability | failed (N1) | N1 |\n| requirements | failed (N1) | N1 |\n| scope | passed | structure:design-83948b834dad4e0e |\n| security | passed | integration:pose-mcp/go/review-brief-conclusion-rules-integration |\n| solution-proportionality | passed | structure:design-83948b834dad4e0e |\n\nR2-N1 is fixed: the reason check rejects punctuation and accepts a reason beginning with a one-letter word. I swept all 18 changed paths, rechecked parsing and ready-check, ADR matching, qualified composite IDs, plan/bundle serialization and digests, brief v11, finding conversion and conclusion blockers, docs/scaffold parity, and the accepted L1/L2 limits. The gate requires a sealed limit ID and rationale; D1 leaves whether a finding semantically falls within that limit to reviewer judgment. L1 discloses the author-controlled breadth and requires disputes to block; L2 is bound into the plan digest and requires a new bundle after edits, so both are justified.\n\n\"'```pose-draft\n{\n  \"schema\": \"pose.review.draft/v1\",\n  \"decision\": \"changes-requested\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N1\",\n      \"severity\": \"medium\",\n      \"disposition\": \"blocker\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits.go\",\n      \"line\": 28,\n      \"summary\": \"The reason matcher searches for Accepted because anywhere in the text and does not require a positive standalone marker. An entry such as '\"'Not accepted because this would violate scope' supplies multiple letter runs after that substring and passes ready-check, allowing a limit whose text rejects its acceptance to be sealed.\\\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \\\"prior_findings\\\": [\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R2-N1\\\",\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"fixed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"go -C pose-mcp test ./internal/pose ./internal/cli -run 'AcceptedLimit|WithinASealedLimit|ReadyCheckJudges|Brief|Conclud'\\\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \\\"sweep\\\": \\\"Reviewed all 18 paths in the subject and the round 3 parser/test delta. Traced accepted-limit parsing and lint diagnostics, ADR coverage, IDs qualified across composite scopes, plan and bundle fields/digests, brief v11, finding-to-attestation conversion, within-limit blockers, closeout, manuals and scaffold parity. Checked the prior finding, both declared limits, and the focused accepted-limit, brief and conclusion tests.\\\",\n  \\\"criteria\\\": [\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assumption-integrity\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N1\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Verified that limits are qualified in composite scopes and sealed into the plan and bundle. L2's post-seal boundary is bound by the digest; L1's author-controlled breadth is disclosed and disputable, but the new matcher can accept a statement that explicitly says a limit is not accepted (N1).\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-concurrency\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Reviewed the parser and review flow changes: they add immutable limit data and no shared mutable state, asynchronous work, or new cancellation/lifecycle path. The sealed pose-mcp unit suite passes.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-contracts\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/review-brief-conclusion-rules-integration\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The v11 brief and attestation represent the sealed limit and finding attribution; new plan/bundle fields are omitted when empty. The sealed integration contract test passes.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-input-errors\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N1\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-integration-impact\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/review-bundle-convergence\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The plan, bundle, brief and attestation consumers remain connected through the review flow. The integration assessment noted unobserved HTTP consumers at /admin/refresh, /healthz and /mcp, outside the changed review-limit paths; the sealed bundle-convergence integration passes.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-observability\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The parser returns a specific diagnostic for limits without a recognized reason, and the conclusion gate names an unsealed limit or missing rationale. The sealed unit suite passes; the N1 false pass is reported separately.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"compatibility\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/review-brief-templates-are-immutable-integration\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The brief contract advances to v11, while empty optional fields remain omitted to preserve older plan and bundle digests. Reviewed the version/digest tests and the sealed immutable-template integration.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"correctness\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N1\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"design-causality\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-83948b834dad4e0e\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"R1 uses parsing and plan/bundle sealing; R2 exposes the snapshot in brief v11; R3 records a distinct within-limit disposition; R4 checks a reason and ADR references. D1 delegates semantic scope classification to the reviewer and requires a sealed ID plus rationale; D2 binds limits to the plan digest and omits empty fields. The sealed design assessment reports no structural deltas.\\\",\n      \\\"mappings\\\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"documentation\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/review-brief-templates-are-immutable-integration\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Reviewed the English and Portuguese manuals and scaffold copies against runtime behavior: the v11 brief, sealed limits and qualified composite IDs are documented consistently. The sealed template parity integration passes.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"operability\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N1\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"requirements\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N1\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"scope\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-83948b834dad4e0e\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The implementation remains within accepted-limit parsing, plan/bundle sealing, brief rendering, finding attribution and readiness linting named by the spec. The design assessment found no structural deltas.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"security\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/review-brief-conclusion-rules-integration\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Reviewed the input and authority boundary. The conclusion gate requires an ID sealed in the bundle and a rationale; an unsealed ID blocks approval. D1 leaves semantic membership to the reviewer, with the brief exposing the declared limit. No path or new authority input is introduced.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"solution-proportionality\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-83948b834dad4e0e\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"One shared parser is the smallest sufficient way to feed readiness, planning and the review brief; optional fields preserve empty-plan and bundle serialization. A separate parser or a threat taxonomy would add duplication or speculative scope. The current marker check needs a positive standalone form. The design would need reconsideration if semantic membership had to be machine-proven rather than reviewer-judged.\\\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \\\"tools\\\": [\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"artifact-check\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:\\\\\\\"\"'$POSE_REVIEW_CLI'\"\\\\\\\" artifact-check --spec pose-review-declared-threat-model --strict\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Ran through the dispatched engine and exited 0. It selected cs-a8bfddf0ae11/head 0c360090a520abee5ca8dae189816fa5b13385ac, not the brief's cs-e21afd956249/head f00c140e5c2fe4c70e1f2c3c4ec40a7bfc34678e, and reported repository-wide orphan warnings; treat this as a successful invocation, not scoped proof.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-design\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-83948b834dad4e0e\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The sealed design evidence passes with no structural deltas. The ad hoc command also observed 18 paths and no deltas, though its reported subject head differed from this brief.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-discover\\\",\n      \\\"component\\\": \\\"pose-mcp\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:\\\\\\\"\"'$POSE_REVIEW_CLI'\"\\\\\\\" assess discover --no-persist --component pose-mcp\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Ran the recommended discovery assessment for pose-mcp; it completed and discovered the component.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-integrate\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/review-bundle-convergence\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Ran the integration assessment. It found three repository-level HTTP consumer references unobserved; those routes are outside the changed review-limit flow, and the relevant sealed bundle-convergence integration passes.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-tech-debt\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"failed\\\